INSERT INTO `resume_analyses` VALUES (44,26,'rCRDlcyUEe2HF2s147oyBHSYzvxuzntwNoEVvQUJ','General','','Siddhartha_Verma_Resume.docx','466343-6095 SIDDHARTHA VERMA Senior Business Development & Key Account Leader\n+91 – 8310168475 / 9632203681 siddharthaverma03@gmail.com Results-driven professional with 15+ years of EXPERIENCE in driving revenue growth and managing high-value accounts across cloud services and IT infrastructure. Proven EXPERTISE in leading cloud migrations, optimizing service delivery, and building strategic partnerships with C-level executives to drive business success .\n536448172472 PROFILE SUMMARY Accomplished Sales and Business Development Leader with EXPERTISE in driving revenue growth and leading high-performance teams in cloud services , IT infrastructure , and digital transformation . Adept at managing multi-million-dollar accounts and delivering strategic solutions.\nSuccessfully managed key accounts valued at $ 17 M+ , including Biocon, Syngene, Nokia, and Flipkart , overseeing end-to-end operations and cultivating long-term partnerships. Skilled in leveraging Global Capability Centers to deliver tailored solutions with a global reach.\nEXPERTISE in securing high-value contracts and negotiating multi-million-dollar deals , specializing in RFP , RFQ , and RFI management. Regular interaction with CXO-level executives , ensuring alignment with strategic goals and fostering strong client relationships.\nProven track record in new business acquisition , achieving 40%+ revenue growth by identifying market opportunities and expanding client portfolios. Focused on long-term strategic relationships and increasing market share through collaboration with Global Capability Centers .\nSkilled in revenue optimization, leading cost-saving initiatives that delivered 20%+ profitability improvements for clients through cloud and data center solutions , with strong support from Global Capability Centers for efficient service delivery.\nInsightful in Program Management, overseeing large-scale cloud migration PROJECTS with a focus on AWS, Azure , and Oracle Cloud , managing PROJECT teams of up to 24 members , and ensuring $7M+ in PROJECT revenue and successful execution.\nExtensive EXPERIENCE in account operations and service delivery management , ensuring 24/7 support for enterprise clients, maintaining high standards of service across AWS, Azure , and Oracle Cloud platforms with seamless collaboration with Global Capability Centers .\n536448168406 Key Deals Biocon Biologics — ₹147 Cr multi-year managed services expansion Nokia — ₹45 Cr data center consolidation (1 6 0 racks)\nFinastra — ₹18 Cr data center consolidation (70 racks)\n536448210282 CORE COMPETENCIES Global Capability Centre (GCC) Engagements Strategic Business Development (Global Accounts)\nKey Account Management Global Stakeholder & CXO Engagement Client Relationship Management & Retention Contract Lifecycle & Commercial Negotiations Revenue Growth & Account Mining Service Delivery Governance (Cloud & Infra)\nCross-Functional Team Collaboration PROJECT & Program Management Global Operations & Delivery Excellence 536448168406 TECHNICAL SKILLS PROJECT Management  MS PROJECT Service Management  ServiceNow Analytics & Reporting  Power BI, Excel (Advanced level)\nCloud Platforms  Azure, AWS CRM & Business Platforms  Salesforce, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Collaboration Tools  MS Teams, Outlook, SharePoint, Zoom 536448168152 EDUCATION 2009: MBA: Business Administration and Management | ICFAI Business School, Pune 2005: Bachelor of Science: Computer Engineering Kalpataru Institute of Technology, Tiptur 536448199643 WORK EXPERIENCE Nov’24 – July`25 | Senior Business Development Manager - Cloud & Managed Service , NTT India Private Limited, Bengaluru Key Account Management: Managed high-value enterprise accounts across GCC, Banking and Life Sciences sectors, New Customer Acquisition: Secured new enterprise clients within 6 months, adding ₹ 2 5+ crore in total contract value by driving tailored sales strategies and consultative engagement.\nRevenue Growth: Drove revenue enhancement initiatives through upselling, cross-selling, and solution-based consultative engagement.\nProposal Management: Created and coordinated tailored responses to RFPs, RFIs, and RFQs, collaborating with technical and delivery teams to craft winning proposals.\nCXO Engagement : Engaged with CXO-level stakeholders to understand business needs, influence decision-making, position value-driven solutions.\nP&L and Account Operations: Oversaw end-to-end account operations including P&L management , delivery governance, and performance monitoring to ensure profitability and service excellence.\nSep’22 – Oct’24 | Associate Manager- Business Development, Client Service, Infosys Ltd., Bengaluru Strategic Account Management: Managed a high-value PORTFOLIO\n, driving client retention, service delivery excellence, and long-term strategic partnerships across Banking and Life Sciences sectors.\nRevenue Growth & New Business: Led new customer acquisition and account mining initiatives, resulting in 15% year-over-year revenue growth through upselling, cross-selling, and consultative selling strategies.\nCXO-Level Stakeholder Engagement: Built and nurtured relationships with CXO-level executives in enterprise accounts, aligning IT solutions with business objectives to drive value and innovation.\nP&L and Operational Oversight: Held end-to-end responsibility for account operations and profitability, ensuring optimized resource utilization, cost control, and timely PROJECT execution.\nProposal Management: Directed RFP/RFI/RFQ response processes in collaboration with delivery and technical teams, crafting customized, client- winning proposals.\nFeb’17 – Aug’22 | Solution Architect & Senior PROJECT Manager, LTI-Mindtree Ltd., Bengaluru, PROJECT Management, Team Handling, Stakeholder Management, Reporting, Handling application hosting, migration, transformation, AWS/Azure of public cloud (AWS/ Azure migration, Fresh Builds) PROJECT\n.\nApr’19 – Aug’22 | Alliance Data Systems – Cloud Operations (Team Size: 24): Led multi-cloud operations across AWS, Oracle Cloud, and Amazon Workspace, driving I infrastructure efficiency, service reliability, and automation to support business continuity and scalability.\nDec’19 – Aug’22 |Interior Specialists Inc – Cloud Operations (Team Size: 8): Oversaw end-to-end cloud infrastructure management on AWS and Oracle Cloud, enhancing system uptime, implementing cost-optimization strategies, and improving operational workflows.\nJan’20 – Apr’20 | ICONIX – Azure DR Migration (Team Size: 6): Directed the complete Disaster Recovery migration to Microsoft Azure, including discovery, design, build, migration, and hypercare, resulting in improved resilience, compliance, and system recoverability.\nApr’18 – Jan’19 | Paraxel – Datacenter to Azure Migration (Team Size: 12): Managed migration of legacy datacenter to Microsoft Azure by leading assessment, architecture design, build, migration, and post-migration hypercare using Azure and RISC tools, enabling cloud agility and cost reduction.\nMay’17 – Dec’17 | Interior Specialists – AWS Migration (Team Size: 9): Spearheaded the company’s first end-to-end datacenter-to-AWS migration PROJECT\n, covering due diligence, planning, AWS setup, data migration, and support.\nJul’13 – Jan’17 | Account Manager, Netmagic Solutions (An NTT Company), Bengaluru Services: Managed Services, Public & Private Cloud, Hybrid Cloud, Managed & Dedicated Hosting, Datacenter, Disaster Recovery, Security Services, SAP Hosting services, Infrastructure management services, Virtualization.\nResponsibilities: Managing large customer, taking care of their new requirements, managing escalations, payment issues, and renewals, and revenue enhancement.\nNew Logo Acquisition: Acquiring new customers, presentation, Pre-Sales consulting, negotiation, and taking the deal to the closure level.\nRevenue Enhancement: Creating a business plan to exceed the revenue target by cross-sell and upsell.\nCXO-Level Stakeholder Engagement: Built and nurtured relationships with CXO-level executives in enterprise accounts, aligning IT solutions with business objectives to drive value and innovation.\nProposal Management: Directed RFP/RFI/RFQ response processes in collaboration with delivery and technical teams, crafting customized, client- winning proposals.\nJan’11 – Jul 13 | Area Sales Manager, Reliance Communication, Bengaluru Services: Data Center, Private cloud, High Speed Internet Access, MPLS VPN, Lease Line, IPLC, Global MPLS, Global Ethernet Lease Line, PRI, Centrex, Global SIM Card, Audio Conferencing Services, and Managed Services Responsibilities: Account Management, New logo acquisition, PROJECT Delivery, Revenue Assurance and Enhancement, Pre- Sales.\nKey Accounts Management: Handling named accounts of Reliance Communications.\nNew Logo Acquisition : Creating new customers and handling existing customers.\nIncreasing Wallet share: Getting business from existing customers Customer Onboarding: Handling service delivery, Revenue assurance, and enhancement.\nCustomer Satisfaction : Ensuring maximum customer satisfaction by closely interacting with potential clients & understanding their requirements and customizing the service accordingly. Handling the complete sales and delivery cycle.\nCXO-Level Stakeholder Engagement: Built and nurtured relationships with CXO-level executives in enterprise accounts, aligning IT solutions with business objectives to drive value and innovation.\nP&L and Operational Oversight: Held end-to-end responsibility for account operations and profitability, ensuring optimized resource utilization, cost control, and timely PROJECT execution.\n536448168747 PREVIOUS EXPERIENCE May’10 – Jun’11 | Key Account Manager, Newwave Computing Pvt Ltd., Bengaluru May’09 – May’10 | International Business Development, AT&T Global| Business Services India Pvt. Ltd.\