space, driving I infrastructure efficiency, service reliability, and automation to support business continuity and scalability.\nDec’19 – Aug’22 |Interior Specialists Inc – Cloud Operations (Team Size: 8): Oversaw end-to-end cloud infrastructure management on AWS and Oracle Cloud, enhancing system uptime, implementing cost-optimization strategies, and improving operational workflows.\nJan’20 – Apr’20 | ICONIX – Azure DR Migration (Team Size: 6): Directed the complete Disaster Recovery migration to Microsoft Azure, including discovery, design, build, migration, and hypercare, resulting in improved resilience, compliance, and system recoverability.\nApr’18 – Jan’19 | Paraxel – Datacenter to Azure Migration (Team Size: 12): Managed migration of legacy datacenter to Microsoft Azure by leading assessment, architecture design, build, migration, and post-migration hypercare using Azure and RISC tools, enabling cloud agility and cost reduction.\nMay’17 – Dec’17 | Interior Specialists – AWS Migration (Team Size: 9): Spearheaded the company’s first end-to-end datacenter-to-AWS migration PROJECT\n, covering due diligence, planning, AWS setup, data migration, and support.\nJul’13 – Jan’17 | Account Manager, Netmagic Solutions (An NTT Company), Bengaluru Services: Managed Services, Public & Private Cloud, Hybrid Cloud, Managed & Dedicated Hosting, Datacenter, Disaster Recovery, Security Services, SAP Hosting services, Infrastructure management services, Virtualization.\nResponsibilities: Managing large customer, taking care of their new requirements, managing escalations, payment issues, and renewals, and revenue enhancement.\nNew Logo Acquisition: Acquiring new customers, presentation, Pre-Sales consulting, negotiation, and taking the deal to the closure level.\nRevenue Enhancement: Creating a business plan to exceed the revenue target by cross-sell and upsell.\nCXO-Level Stakeholder Engagement: Built and nurtured relationships with CXO-level executives in enterprise accounts, 